# Graph Convolutional Network (GCN) Framework

A PyTorch implementation of a static Graph Convolutional Network for graph-level classification tasks.

## Overview

The static GCN framework provides a complete pipeline for graph classification with:
- **Graph Convolutional Layers**: Multi-layer GCN with residual connections and layer normalization
- **Graph-level Pooling**: Attention-based aggregation of node features to graph embeddings
- **Classification Head**: MLP classifier for graph-level predictions
- **5-Fold Cross-Validation**: Automated training and evaluation pipeline

This framework is ideal for classifying individual static graphs (single snapshots) with flexible node feature support.

## Features

- ✅ Multi-layer GCN with layer normalization and residual connections
- ✅ Attention-based graph-level pooling
- ✅ Support for custom node features (default or pre-computed)
- ✅ 5-fold cross-validation training loop
- ✅ Automatic feature dimension detection
- ✅ String label support with automatic numeric class mapping
- ✅ Flexible directory-based data organization
- ✅ Batch processing with padding support
- ✅ Built-in model checkpointing

## Directory Structure

Organize your data as follows:

```
.
├── datasets/              # Dataset definition files
│   └── dataset_name.txt   # Format: <label> <sample_name> per line
├── graphs/                # Graph data for each sample
│   ├── sample1.npy        # or .txt, .npz
│   ├── sample2.npy
│   ├── sample3.npy
│   └── ...
├── features/              # Node features (optional)
│   ├── sample1_features.npy
│   ├── sample2_features.npy
│   └── ...
├── partitions/            # 5-fold partition definitions
│   └── dataset_name/
│       ├── 1  # Format: one sample name per line
│       ├── 2
│       ├── 3
│       ├── 4
│       └── 5
├── GCN.py
└── README_GCN.md
```

## Dataset File Format

**datasets/your_dataset.txt**:
```
class_A sample1
class_B sample2
class_A sample3
class_C sample4
```

Labels can be:
- Numeric: `0 sample1`, `1 sample2`
- Strings: `positive sample1`, `negative sample2`
- Any non-numeric identifiers

Labels are automatically mapped to integer classes (0, 1, 2, ...).

## Partition Files Format

**partitions/dataset_name/1** (and 2, 3, 4, 5):
```
sample1
sample3
sample7
sample12
```

Each fold file contains one sample name per line.

## Adjacency Matrix Formats

Graph files can be in:
- **NumPy arrays**: `.npy` or `.npz` (2D square matrices for adjacency)
- **Text files**: `.txt` with space/comma-separated values
- **Edge lists**: 2 columns (u, v) pairs; auto-converted to adjacency matrix

## Node Features Formats

Feature files can be:
- **NumPy arrays**: `.npy` or `.npz` with shape [num_nodes, feature_dim]
- **Text files**: `.txt` with one node per line, space/comma-separated values
- **Missing**: Defaults to ones vector [num_nodes, 1]

